000100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000200 PROGRAM-ID. USEVSAM.
000300* Relative and Indexed I-O level 1: USE AFTER STANDARD ERROR
000400* PROCEDURE ON a KSDS and on an RRDS. A READ with no INVALID KEY
000500* of a record that is not there sets FILE STATUS, runs the USE
000600* procedure, and continues with the next statement; a READ that
000700* finds its record does not touch the procedure. One declarative
000800* names its file, the other applies by mode.
000900 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
001000 INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
001100 FILE-CONTROL.
001200     SELECT KSDS-FILE ASSIGN TO KSDSF01
001300         ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
001400         ACCESS IS RANDOM
001500         RECORD KEY IS KR-KEY
001600         FILE STATUS IS KS.
001700     SELECT RRDS-FILE ASSIGN TO RRDSF01
001800         ORGANIZATION IS RELATIVE
001900         ACCESS IS RANDOM
002000         RELATIVE KEY IS RR-NUM
002100         FILE STATUS IS RS.
002200 DATA DIVISION.
002300 FILE SECTION.
002400 FD  KSDS-FILE
002500     LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD
002600     RECORD CONTAINS 80 CHARACTERS.
002700 01  KSDS-RECORD.
002800     02  KR-KEY                  PIC X(10).
002900     02  FILLER                  PIC X(70).
003000 FD  RRDS-FILE
003100     LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD
003200     RECORD CONTAINS 80 CHARACTERS.
003300 01  RRDS-RECORD                 PIC X(80).
003400 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
003500 01  KS                          PIC XX VALUE '00'.
003600 01  RS                          PIC XX VALUE '00'.
003700 01  RR-NUM                      PIC 9(8) COMP VALUE 0.
003800 01  K-USE                       PIC 9 VALUE 0.
003900 01  R-USE                       PIC 9 VALUE 0.
004000 01  SAVE-KEY                    PIC X(10).
004100 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
004200 DECLARATIVES.
004300 K-ERR SECTION.
004400     USE AFTER STANDARD ERROR PROCEDURE ON KSDS-FILE.
004500 K-ERR-P.
004600     ADD 1 TO K-USE.
004700     DISPLAY 'KSDS USE: STATUS ' KS.
004800 R-ERR SECTION.
004900     USE AFTER STANDARD ERROR PROCEDURE ON I-O.
005000 R-ERR-P.
005100     ADD 1 TO R-USE.
005200     DISPLAY 'RRDS USE: STATUS ' RS.
005300 END DECLARATIVES.
005400 MAIN SECTION.
005500 MAIN-P.
005600     OPEN INPUT KSDS-FILE.
005700     OPEN I-O RRDS-FILE.
005800     MOVE ALL 'Z' TO KR-KEY.
005900     READ KSDS-FILE.
006000     DISPLAY 'AFTER BAD KSDS READ: STATUS ' KS ' USE ' K-USE.
006100     MOVE 1 TO RR-NUM.
006200     READ RRDS-FILE.
006300     DISPLAY 'AFTER GOOD RRDS READ: STATUS ' RS ' USE ' R-USE.
006400     MOVE 99999 TO RR-NUM.
006500     READ RRDS-FILE.
006600     DISPLAY 'AFTER BAD RRDS READ: STATUS ' RS ' USE ' R-USE.
006700     MOVE ALL 'Z' TO KR-KEY.
006800     READ KSDS-FILE INVALID KEY DISPLAY 'INVALID KEY TAKEN'.
006900     DISPLAY 'WITH A PHRASE: USE ' K-USE.
007000     CLOSE KSDS-FILE RRDS-FILE.
007100     STOP RUN.
